From: Shirogane Tsumugi <artoriapendragon123@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] spi: sun6i: move the read sample point with the bus speed

SPI_TCR has two bits controlling when the master samples MISO, and the
driver leaves both at zero regardless of speed. That happens to be the
right setting for the middle of the range, which is why this has never
been noticed, but it does not hold at either end.

Past roughly 60MHz the round trip -- SCLK propagating to the slave and its
data coming back -- no longer fits inside the setup time, and SDC (bit 11)
has to delay the sample point by half an SCLK cycle. Below roughly 24MHz
the default delay is itself the problem and SDM (bit 13) selects plain
sampling instead. Manual 7.3.7.2 documents both; the thresholds are the
ones the BSP driver applies in sunxi_spi_mode_check().

This matters on suniv now: the CDR2 divider hangs off the 200MHz AHB, so
the reachable rates are 100/50/33MHz and nothing in between. Asking for
anything under 100 lands on 50, which sits in the no-adjustment window --
but 100MHz needs SDC, so the frequency cannot be raised without this.

Signed-off-by: Shirogane Tsumugi <artoriapendragon123@gmail.com>

--- a/drivers/spi/spi-sun6i.c
+++ b/drivers/spi/spi-sun6i.c
@@ -43,9 +43,15 @@
 #define SUN6I_TFR_CTL_CS_MANUAL			BIT(6)
 #define SUN6I_TFR_CTL_CS_LEVEL			BIT(7)
 #define SUN6I_TFR_CTL_DHB			BIT(8)
+#define SUN6I_TFR_CTL_SDC			BIT(11)
 #define SUN6I_TFR_CTL_FBS			BIT(12)
+#define SUN6I_TFR_CTL_SDM			BIT(13)
 #define SUN6I_TFR_CTL_XCH			BIT(31)
 
+/* Speeds at which the read sample point has to move, as used by the BSP */
+#define SUN6I_SPI_HIGH_FREQ		60000000
+#define SUN6I_SPI_LOW_FREQ		24000000
+
 #define SUN6I_INT_CTL_REG		0x10
 #define SUN6I_INT_CTL_RF_RDY			BIT(0)
 #define SUN6I_INT_CTL_TF_ERQ			BIT(4)
@@ -260,6 +266,20 @@
 	}
 
 	sun6i_spi_write(sspi, SUN6I_CLK_CTL_REG, reg);
+
+	/*
+	 * Past a point the round trip of SCLK going out and the slave's data
+	 * coming back no longer fits in the setup time, so the sample point has
+	 * to move half a cycle later; slow buses want it moved the other way.
+	 * The thresholds are the ones the BSP driver uses.
+	 */
+	reg = sun6i_spi_read(sspi, SUN6I_TFR_CTL_REG);
+	reg &= ~(SUN6I_TFR_CTL_SDC | SUN6I_TFR_CTL_SDM);
+	if (speed_hz >= SUN6I_SPI_HIGH_FREQ)
+		reg |= SUN6I_TFR_CTL_SDC;
+	else if (speed_hz <= SUN6I_SPI_LOW_FREQ)
+		reg |= SUN6I_TFR_CTL_SDM;
+	sun6i_spi_write(sspi, SUN6I_TFR_CTL_REG, reg);
 }
 
 static void sun6i_spi_dma_rx_cb(void *param)
